 "2026-08-29T23:07:21.919618499Z", :host "rehydrated isolated Linux x64 worktree; Clojure CLI tools jar 1.12.5.1664; OpenJDK 17.0.20; Node 24.19.0", :kind :test-run, :origin "open-hax/katamorph#26", :owner "codex/katamorph22-publish"}
{:pi "foresight-constellation-zero-inbox", :refs "pr13-head:aaafeba49a1c3cf457d6c32b06fe62d0e4e93483,coderabbit-review:5059477323,threads:PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddeEC|PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddeED", :dod "Reject malformed binding registries and disabled host providers before candidate selection", :manifest "src/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry_shape.cljc,src/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry.cljc,test/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry_test.cljc,.ημ/receipts.edn", :note "Fresh exact-head CodeRabbit review found that nil, sequential, and scalar binding registries could be accepted or throw instead of failing closed, and that an enabled binding still returned a host provider explicitly marked :enabled false. The repair requires a map registry before entry validation and excludes candidates when either the binding or referenced provider is explicitly disabled. Default absence of either flag remains enabled.", :tests "RED JVM: 65 tests/254 assertions, 5 failures and 1 error reproducing nil/vector/scalar registry acceptance or throw plus disabled-provider selection; GREEN JVM: 65 tests/257 assertions, 0 failures/errors; GREEN full clj-kondo: 0 errors/warnings; GREEN git diff --check; BLOCKED isolated clojure -Srepro and local CLJS before project load because the expired Maven proxy could not restore an uncached transitive dependency, so exact-head hosted checks and fresh review remain mandatory", :ts "2026-08-29T23:46:11.281579630Z", :host "isolated Linux x64 worktree; direct cached JVM classpath with Clojure 1.12.5 and Malli 0.16.4; clj-kondo 2026.08.04", :kind :test-run, :origin "open-hax/katamorph#13", :owner "codex/katamorph-finish"}
{:pi "foresight-constellation-zero-inbox", :refs "pr13-head:a3ad17eb867ab04bcd0c4e2473b0ed6bf77b97af,codex-review:5059491049,threads:PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddeTa|PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddeTc|PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddeTe|PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddgTx", :dod "Make provider lookup fail closed and candidate ordering total for every valid contract-id type", :manifest "src/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry_shape.cljc,src/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry.cljc,test/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry_test.cljc,.ημ/receipts.edn", :note "Fresh successor reviews found that compose still scanned conflicts eagerly after detecting a scalar registry, unknown queried action IDs were indistinguishable from valid actions with no bindings, and keyword/string binding IDs with the same printed form made stable sorting depend on map iteration order. The repair short-circuits invalid composition, returns a structured unknown-action error before candidate selection, and sorts by contract-id type plus text. A fourth thread repeated the already-closed non-map validation case; exact-head code and nil/vector/scalar regressions disprove it, so no duplicate code change was made.", :tests "RED JVM: 67 tests/262 assertions, 3 failures and 1 error reproducing eager scalar conflict scanning, unknown-action success, and type-colliding order drift; GREEN JVM: 67 tests/262 assertions, 0 failures/errors; GREEN full clj-kondo: 0 errors/warnings; GREEN git diff --check; exact-head hosted checks and fresh review remain mandatory", :ts "2026-08-29T23:53:27.183539528Z", :host "isolated Linux x64 worktree; direct cached JVM classpath with Clojure 1.12.5 and Malli 0.16.4; clj-kondo 2026.08.04", :kind :test-run, :origin "open-hax/katamorph#13", :owner "codex/katamorph-finish"}
{:pi "foresight-constellation-zero-inbox", :refs "pr13-head:fabd89878ba85c98af88a2d2e95fba0b84cbb3ee,codex-review:5059503659,thread:PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddinJ", :dod "Reject falsey provider registry entries before candidate selection", :manifest "src/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry.cljc,test/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry_test.cljc,.ημ/receipts.edn", :note "Fresh exact-head Codex review found that key presence alone treated nil and false provider values as resolved, allowing an unusable provider registry entry to yield a successful candidate. The repair requires the referenced registry value itself to be truthy. Provider maps remain eligible by default, while maps explicitly marked :enabled false continue to be excluded during candidate selection.", :tests "RED JVM: 67 tests/266 assertions, 4 failures reproducing nil and false provider acceptance; GREEN JVM: 67 tests/266 assertions, 0 failures/errors; GREEN full clj-kondo: 0 errors/warnings; GREEN git diff --check; exact-head hosted checks and fresh review remain mandatory", :ts "2026-08-30T00:01:45.565716218Z", :host "isolated Linux x64 worktree; direct cached JVM classpath with Clojure 1.12.5 and Malli 0.16.4; clj-kondo 2026.08.04", :kind :test-run, :origin "open-hax/katamorph#13", :owner "codex/katamorph-finish"}
{:pi "foresight-constellation-zero-inbox", :refs "pr13-head:4d9c181f114d87772a793cf843cd7be24795e85d,codex-review:5059521799,thread:PRRT_kwDOTWpA986ddlRc", :dod "Reject false action registry entries in both binding and queried-action resolution", :manifest "src/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry.cljc,test/cljc/katamorph/action/binding_registry_test.cljc,.ημ/receipts.edn", :note "Fresh exact-head Codex review found that nil-only action resolution treated a false registry entry as a valid ActionSemantics contract. The repair applies the same truthiness law already used for provider values in reference validation and direct queried-action resolution. Regressions cover both binding resolution and candidate lookup while retaining the existing structured behavior for nil or missing actions.", :tests "RED JVM: 67 tests/272 assertions, 4 failures reproducing false action acceptance in bind and providers-for; GREEN JVM: 67 tests/272 assertions, 0 failures/errors; GREEN full clj-kondo: 0 errors/warnings; GREEN git diff --check; exact-head hosted checks and fresh review remain mandatory", :ts "2026-08-30T00:09:04.743456089Z", :host "isolated Linux x64 worktree; direct cached JVM classpath with Clojure 1.12.5 and Malli 0.16.4; clj-kondo 2026.08.04", :kind :test-run, :origin "open-hax/katamorph#13", :owner "codex/katamorph-finish"}
